A monk's connection to Void-the instinctual and correct reaction in a
given situation-is negatively affected by attachment to physical items
and things, and emotional biases unbalanced by reason (and
vice-versa).

So, I'm thinking of a patch that mimics this by cloning some of luck's
mechanisms, and giving monks a variable modifier that is used when an
instinctual or habitual reaction is called for.

Anyone have any other ideas, or think that this would be too
unbalancing?  I considered changing half the luck mechanism (moreluck)
to be Void instead, but it seems easier to code-and control the scope
of the change-if I add a new variable.

DETAILS SPOILER:

My current idea is to start with add a modifier from +5 to -5,
depending on how many items are in the monk's inventory (every five
items subtracts one point), and then add in any modifiers to the
monk's mental state (eg, decrease for confusion or hallucination,
increase for warning or clairvoyance).

